WEBVTT

1
00:00:11,646 --> 00:00:17,084
[Elvis Presley]
<i>♪ For I can't help ♪</i>

2
00:00:17,184 --> 00:00:21,488
<i>♪ Falling in love ♪</i>

3
00:00:21,589 --> 00:00:25,492
<i>♪ With ♪</i>

4
00:00:25,593 --> 00:00:28,696
<i>♪ You... ♪</i>

5
00:00:30,063 --> 00:00:31,733
[crowd roaring distantly]

6
00:00:31,833 --> 00:00:33,367
[Elvis Presley] I'd like
to talk to you a little bit,

7
00:00:33,467 --> 00:00:35,737
ladies and gentlemen, about
how I got in this business.

8
00:00:36,136 --> 00:00:37,204
There's been a lot written
and a lot said,

9
00:00:37,304 --> 00:00:39,139
but never from my
side of the story.

10
00:00:39,239 --> 00:00:42,777
[roaring crowd increasing]

11
00:00:43,645 --> 00:00:47,247
["Also Sprach Zarathustra"
by Richard Strauss playing]

12
00:00:50,752 --> 00:00:54,087
[crowd cheering]

13
00:00:54,321 --> 00:00:56,290
[Elvis] People can stay home
and hear you sing,

14
00:00:56,390 --> 00:00:57,992
but when they pay
their money to come out

15
00:00:58,091 --> 00:01:00,227
and see you
on a personal appearance,

16
00:01:00,327 --> 00:01:02,095
those people
want to see a show.

17
00:01:03,196 --> 00:01:04,933
They come out
to see some action.

18
00:01:05,033 --> 00:01:08,235
["Also Sprach Zarathustra"
continues]

19
00:01:08,335 --> 00:01:11,271
[interviewer] Elvis Presley
is a no talent performer,

20
00:01:11,371 --> 00:01:14,576
riding the crest of a wave
of mass hysteria.

21
00:01:14,676 --> 00:01:17,244
How's your feeling on that -
no talent performer?

22
00:01:17,344 --> 00:01:19,914
[Elvis] I don't know, I don't
even want to think about it.

23
00:01:20,014 --> 00:01:21,448
[man] He ain't nothing
but an idiot.

24
00:01:21,549 --> 00:01:23,518
["Also Sprach Zarathustra"
concluding]

25
00:01:23,618 --> 00:01:26,253
[crowd roaring]

26
00:01:33,427 --> 00:01:36,864
[band playing
"Battle Hymn of the Republic"]

27
00:01:44,639 --> 00:01:46,874
<i>♪ Glory, glory ♪</i>

28
00:01:46,975 --> 00:01:52,279
<i>♪ Hallelujah ♪</i>

29
00:01:52,379 --> 00:01:54,749
<i>♪ His truth ♪</i>

30
00:01:54,849 --> 00:01:58,686
<i>♪ Is marching ♪</i>

31
00:01:58,786 --> 00:02:03,758
<i>♪ On ♪</i>

32
00:02:03,858 --> 00:02:09,764
<i>♪ His truth is marching ♪</i>

33
00:02:09,864 --> 00:02:16,638
<i>♪ On... ♪</i>

34
00:02:19,339 --> 00:02:23,410
-[song concludes]
-[crowd cheering]

35
00:02:25,747 --> 00:02:28,215
["Baby Let's Play House"
by Elvis Presley playing]

36
00:02:32,352 --> 00:02:34,321
[Elvis]
Hi, this is Elvis Presley.

37
00:02:34,421 --> 00:02:36,189
I guess the first thing
people want to know

38
00:02:36,289 --> 00:02:37,925
is why I can't stand still
when I'm singing.

39
00:02:39,661 --> 00:02:42,030
Some people tap their feet,
some people snap their fingers

40
00:02:42,130 --> 00:02:44,132
and some people just
sway back and forth.

41
00:02:44,766 --> 00:02:47,035
I just sort of do them
all together, I guess.

42
00:02:47,467 --> 00:02:49,037
Singing Rhythm and Blues
really knocks it out.

43
00:02:49,137 --> 00:02:50,437
Knocks it out...

44
00:02:50,538 --> 00:02:52,439
<i>♪ Oh, baby, baby</i>
<i>Baby, baby, baby ♪</i>

45
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:54,809
[Elvis] I watch my audience
and listen to them

46
00:02:54,909 --> 00:02:56,711
and I know that we're
all getting something

47
00:02:56,811 --> 00:02:58,846
out of our system, and
none of us knows what it is.

48
00:02:58,946 --> 00:03:01,448
<i>♪ Come back, baby</i>
<i>I want to play house with you ♪</i>

49
00:03:01,549 --> 00:03:03,051
[Elvis] The important thing is
that we're getting rid of it

50
00:03:03,151 --> 00:03:04,719
and nobody's getting hurt.

51
00:03:05,687 --> 00:03:07,354
Rock and Roll Music, if you
like it and if you feel it,

52
00:03:07,454 --> 00:03:09,123
you can't help but move to it.

53
00:03:09,222 --> 00:03:11,458
That's what happens to me,
I can't help it.

54
00:03:11,559 --> 00:03:13,594
I mean, I have to move around,
I can't stand still.

55
00:03:13,695 --> 00:03:15,730
I've tried it
and I can't do it.

56
00:03:15,830 --> 00:03:17,632
<i>♪ Well, it's one for the money</i>
<i>Two for the show ♪</i>

57
00:03:17,732 --> 00:03:19,834
Man, I was tame
compared to what they do now.

58
00:03:19,934 --> 00:03:21,334
Are you kidding? [laughs]

59
00:03:21,435 --> 00:03:23,638
I didn't do anything,
I would just jiggle, you know?

60
00:03:24,806 --> 00:03:27,240
I get in kind of rhythm
with the music,

61
00:03:27,340 --> 00:03:29,644
jump around to it because
I enjoy what I'm doing.

62
00:03:29,744 --> 00:03:32,446
I'm not trying to be vulgar,
I'm not trying to sell any sex.

63
00:03:33,213 --> 00:03:34,849
<i>♪ Oh, walk the dog ♪</i>

64
00:03:34,949 --> 00:03:37,518
[interviewer] When did you
first start singing?

65
00:03:37,618 --> 00:03:39,520
Do you call it 'singing',
the stuff you do?

66
00:03:39,620 --> 00:03:41,522
<i>♪ Baby, if I made you mad ♪</i>

67
00:03:41,622 --> 00:03:42,757
[Elvis] Do I call it singing?

68
00:03:42,857 --> 00:03:43,791
[interviewer] Yeah, that is
what you call it, right?

69
00:03:43,891 --> 00:03:45,927
[Elvis] Well, I've sold
five million records.

70
00:03:46,027 --> 00:03:47,294
Somebody calls it singing.

71
00:03:49,463 --> 00:03:52,066
["Shake, Rattle and Roll"
by Elvis Presley playing]

72
00:03:52,533 --> 00:03:53,901
[Elvis]
So, that's how it happens -

73
00:03:54,001 --> 00:03:55,903
you get a record
and then you get on television,

74
00:03:56,003 --> 00:03:57,437
and you go to Hollywood, so...

75
00:03:57,538 --> 00:03:59,040
So I wasn't ready for that town

76
00:03:59,140 --> 00:04:00,608
and they wasn't ready for me,
you know.

77
00:04:00,708 --> 00:04:02,977
<i>♪ Well, I said</i>
<i>shake, rattle and roll ♪</i>

78
00:04:03,077 --> 00:04:06,514
<i>♪ Crawfish ♪</i>

79
00:04:06,614 --> 00:04:08,549
[Elvis] I went to Hollywood
and I made "Love Me Tender",

80
00:04:08,649 --> 00:04:11,185
"Loving You" and loving her...

81
00:04:11,318 --> 00:04:14,354
Loving whoever I could get my
hands on at the time, you know.

82
00:04:14,454 --> 00:04:16,524
And then I did "King Creole",

83
00:04:16,624 --> 00:04:19,392
so I was really getting used to
the Hollywood bit, you know.

84
00:04:19,493 --> 00:04:21,229
I had a Cadillac
and I had sunglasses on.

85
00:04:21,328 --> 00:04:22,496
I'm sitting in the back seat,
saying,

86
00:04:22,597 --> 00:04:24,264
"I'm a movie star,
I'm a somebody."

87
00:04:26,067 --> 00:04:27,969
<i>♪ Sad sack was sitting</i>
<i>on a block of stone ♪</i>

88
00:04:28,069 --> 00:04:29,604
[interviewer] There is
quite a group of people

89
00:04:29,704 --> 00:04:31,271
who don't sort of approve
of the thing you do.

90
00:04:31,371 --> 00:04:33,241
They seem to think
that it contributes

91
00:04:33,340 --> 00:04:35,308
to juvenile delinquency
and all sorts of things.

92
00:04:35,408 --> 00:04:37,011
You given any thoughts to, uh,

93
00:04:37,111 --> 00:04:38,780
the unpopular side
of your audience?

94
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:40,915
[Elvis] Yes, sir, I have.
I've tried to figure it out.

95
00:04:41,015 --> 00:04:42,517
I don't see how they can think

96
00:04:42,617 --> 00:04:44,519
that it would contribute
to juvenile delinquency.

97
00:04:44,619 --> 00:04:47,722
Someone solely singing
and dancing, I don't see that.

98
00:04:47,822 --> 00:04:50,558
<i>♪ You ain't nothin'</i>
<i>but a hound dog ♪</i>

99
00:04:50,658 --> 00:04:52,727
<i>♪ Crying all the time ♪</i>

100
00:04:52,827 --> 00:04:55,163
And I believe
with all of my heart

101
00:04:55,263 --> 00:04:57,231
that it is
a contributing factor

102
00:04:57,330 --> 00:04:59,432
to our juvenile delinquency
of today.

103
00:04:59,534 --> 00:05:01,569
<i>[Elvis] ♪ I've got</i>
<i>a dirty, dirty feeling ♪</i>

104
00:05:01,669 --> 00:05:03,303
[man] Why I believe that is
because I know how it feels

105
00:05:03,403 --> 00:05:04,539
when you're singing.

106
00:05:04,639 --> 00:05:06,473
[Elvis] For one,
I have a very bad temper.

107
00:05:06,574 --> 00:05:08,743
-I know what it does to you.
-[Elvis] Extremely bad temper.

108
00:05:08,843 --> 00:05:11,712
Of the evil feeling
that you feel when you sing,

109
00:05:11,813 --> 00:05:14,649
the lust position that
you get into in the beat.

110
00:05:14,749 --> 00:05:16,584
If you talk to the average
teenager of today

111
00:05:16,684 --> 00:05:18,385
and you ask them what it is

112
00:05:18,485 --> 00:05:20,320
about Rock and Roll Music
that they like,

113
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:23,490
the first thing they'll say is,
"The beat, the beat, the beat."

114
00:05:23,591 --> 00:05:26,260
It happened so fast, it's hard
to keep up with it, you know.

115
00:05:26,359 --> 00:05:27,962
It's just, boom, overnight
and there it was.

116
00:05:28,062 --> 00:05:29,831
[Elvis] It happened very fast
to all of us,

117
00:05:29,931 --> 00:05:32,266
my mother and my father
and all of us that...

118
00:05:32,365 --> 00:05:34,135
you know,
everything happened overnight.

119
00:05:34,235 --> 00:05:36,871
And so we had to adjust to
a lot of things very quickly.

120
00:05:37,305 --> 00:05:38,338
A lot of good things.

121
00:05:38,438 --> 00:05:40,308
[crowd cheering]

122
00:05:40,407 --> 00:05:41,474
[Vernon Presley]
I have seen his clothes

123
00:05:41,576 --> 00:05:42,944
completely torn off.

124
00:05:44,545 --> 00:05:47,014
Scratched all over, bleeding.

125
00:05:47,347 --> 00:05:49,116
Just wild fans, you know.

126
00:05:49,217 --> 00:05:50,751
[ominous music playing]

127
00:05:50,852 --> 00:05:52,220
[phone ringing]

128
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:54,387
I have Elvis Presley
on the phone. Hello?

129
00:05:54,487 --> 00:05:55,422
[man] Hello.

130
00:05:55,523 --> 00:05:56,824
[woman] Hello, Elvis.
Just one moment.

131
00:05:56,924 --> 00:05:57,892
[man] Hello, Elvis.

132
00:05:57,992 --> 00:05:59,527
Your style of gyrating
while you sing

133
00:05:59,627 --> 00:06:01,262
has been bitterly criticised,

134
00:06:01,361 --> 00:06:04,165
even by usually mild
and gentle TV critics.

135
00:06:04,265 --> 00:06:05,533
Do you think
you've learned anything

136
00:06:05,633 --> 00:06:07,335
from the criticism
levelled at you?

137
00:06:07,434 --> 00:06:09,003
-No, I haven't.
-[man] You haven't, huh?

138
00:06:09,103 --> 00:06:11,973
Because I don't feel
I'm doing anything wrong.

139
00:06:12,306 --> 00:06:13,641
If there's anything
I've tried to do,

140
00:06:13,741 --> 00:06:16,376
I've tried to live
a straight, clean life

141
00:06:16,476 --> 00:06:18,679
and not set any kind
of a bad example.

142
00:06:18,779 --> 00:06:21,649
I will say that
there are people

143
00:06:21,749 --> 00:06:23,718
that are going to like you
and people that don't like you

144
00:06:23,818 --> 00:06:26,486
regardless of what business
you're in or what you do.

145
00:06:26,587 --> 00:06:28,455
You cannot please everyone.

146
00:06:28,556 --> 00:06:30,057
[man] But what about
the rumour

147
00:06:30,157 --> 00:06:31,424
that you once shot your mother?

148
00:06:31,525 --> 00:06:33,227
[chuckling]

149
00:06:33,861 --> 00:06:35,830
Well, I think that one
takes the cake.

150
00:06:38,165 --> 00:06:41,302
<i>♪ Well, since my baby left me ♪</i>

151
00:06:41,401 --> 00:06:44,739
<i>♪ Well, I found</i>
<i>a new place to dwell ♪</i>

152
00:06:44,839 --> 00:06:48,175
[Elvis] And then right when I
was going good, I get drafted.

153
00:06:49,744 --> 00:06:52,380
And overnight it was all gone.
It was like a dream.

154
00:06:52,479 --> 00:06:55,316
[snaps fingers] Pah! Changed.

155
00:06:56,050 --> 00:06:57,652
[interviewer] Do you feel
that rock and roll,

156
00:06:57,752 --> 00:06:59,520
the popularity
of rock and roll,

157
00:06:59,620 --> 00:07:01,222
will diminish in any way
while you're in the army?

158
00:07:01,322 --> 00:07:02,390
[Elvis] Well, sir,

159
00:07:02,489 --> 00:07:05,259
rock and roll has been around
for many years.

160
00:07:05,359 --> 00:07:07,895
It used to be called
Rhythm and Blues,

161
00:07:07,995 --> 00:07:11,098
and as far back as I can
remember, it's been very big.

162
00:07:11,198 --> 00:07:13,968
Although, in the last five
years it's gotten much bigger.

163
00:07:14,068 --> 00:07:17,004
I personally don't think it
will ever die completely out,

164
00:07:17,104 --> 00:07:18,973
because they're going to have
to get something mighty good

165
00:07:19,073 --> 00:07:21,509
to take its place as far as the
young people are concerned.

166
00:07:21,609 --> 00:07:25,478
Maybe someday I can come
back when my army tour is up,

167
00:07:25,579 --> 00:07:28,716
as an entertainer,
and then I'll have more time

168
00:07:28,816 --> 00:07:30,685
and maybe I'll have
an opportunity

169
00:07:30,785 --> 00:07:33,321
to kind of make myself
at home over here.

170
00:07:33,421 --> 00:07:35,589
Arrivederci!
No, that's Italian.

171
00:07:35,690 --> 00:07:37,591
[audience laughing]

172
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:41,595
Have two years of
sobering army life

173
00:07:41,696 --> 00:07:44,065
changed your mind
about rock and roll?

174
00:07:44,532 --> 00:07:46,834
"Sobering army life"?
[chuckles]

175
00:07:47,335 --> 00:07:50,671
Uh... no, it hasn't. It hasn't.

176
00:07:50,771 --> 00:07:52,873
It hasn't changed my mind,
because...

177
00:07:52,974 --> 00:07:55,676
I was in tanks for a long time,
you see,

178
00:07:55,776 --> 00:07:58,546
and they rock and roll
quite a bit.

179
00:07:58,646 --> 00:08:00,480
-Fire!
-On the way!

180
00:08:00,581 --> 00:08:02,750
-[explosion booming]
<i>-♪ Girls! Girls! Girls! ♪</i>

181
00:08:02,850 --> 00:08:04,785
<i>-♪ Girls ♪</i>
<i>-♪ Going swimming ♪</i>

182
00:08:04,885 --> 00:08:06,787
<i>-♪ Girls ♪</i>
<i>-♪ In bikinis ♪</i>

183
00:08:06,887 --> 00:08:08,322
<i>-♪ Girls ♪</i>
<i>-♪ Walking and a-wiggling by ♪</i>

184
00:08:08,422 --> 00:08:11,559
[announcer] It's a new Elvis,
one you've never seen before.

185
00:08:11,659 --> 00:08:12,893
<i>♪ She said,</i>
<i>"Hey, bossa nova, baby ♪</i>

186
00:08:12,994 --> 00:08:15,629
<i>♪ "Keep on working for</i>
<i>this ain't no time to quit" ♪</i>

187
00:08:15,730 --> 00:08:17,631
<i>♪ She said,</i>
<i>"Go, bossa nova, baby ♪</i>

188
00:08:17,732 --> 00:08:20,034
<i>♪ "Keep on dancing, I'm about</i>
<i>to have myself a fit" ♪</i>

189
00:08:20,901 --> 00:08:25,473
<i>♪ Bossa nova, bossa nova ♪</i>

190
00:08:25,573 --> 00:08:26,907
[Elvis] For a while
there was a theory

191
00:08:27,008 --> 00:08:28,876
that anything I did
would sell and so forth.

192
00:08:28,976 --> 00:08:30,644
Well, I knew that was not true.

193
00:08:30,745 --> 00:08:32,246
Whether it's a song,
a script or whatever,

194
00:08:32,346 --> 00:08:33,714
it's got to be good.

195
00:08:34,915 --> 00:08:36,817
[dog] Wake up, Greg. It's
time to head for the hills.

196
00:08:36,917 --> 00:08:39,453
You can't talk, you're a dog!

197
00:08:39,887 --> 00:08:42,456
[Elvis] Hollywood's image of me
was wrong, and I knew it,

198
00:08:42,556 --> 00:08:44,225
and I couldn't say
anything about it.

199
00:08:44,325 --> 00:08:46,827
[bass guitar riff]

200
00:08:47,495 --> 00:08:48,996
[Elvis] Couldn't do
anything about it.

201
00:08:49,330 --> 00:08:50,698
[tyres squealing]

202
00:08:52,333 --> 00:08:55,202
[Elvis] It's nobody's fault
maybe, except my own.

203
00:08:55,302 --> 00:08:58,906
A lot of times the things
that I didn't fully believe in.

204
00:09:00,274 --> 00:09:02,777
And I was doing a lot of
pictures close together

205
00:09:02,877 --> 00:09:04,445
and the pictures
got very similar.

206
00:09:04,545 --> 00:09:05,613
[tyres squealing]

207
00:09:05,713 --> 00:09:09,450
<i>♪ Girls! Girls! Girls! ♪</i>

208
00:09:09,817 --> 00:09:11,619
[Elvis] So I'd read the
first four or five pages

209
00:09:11,719 --> 00:09:14,822
and I knew that it was
just a different name

210
00:09:14,922 --> 00:09:18,793
with 12 new songs and
I had to gear down

211
00:09:18,893 --> 00:09:20,895
'cause I had to sing to a dog.

212
00:09:20,995 --> 00:09:24,698
[backup singers]
<i>♪ The edge of reality ♪</i>

213
00:09:25,633 --> 00:09:30,638
<i>♪ The edge of reality ♪</i>

214
00:09:30,738 --> 00:09:32,807
[Elvis] I had thought that they
would give me a chance

215
00:09:32,907 --> 00:09:34,842
to show some kind of
acting ability.

216
00:09:34,942 --> 00:09:36,877
[woman] Oh, I mean business.

217
00:09:36,977 --> 00:09:38,746
[Elvis] But it did not change.

218
00:09:38,846 --> 00:09:41,215
It did not change.

219
00:09:41,949 --> 00:09:44,685
I was so concerned that
that's all I talked about.

220
00:09:44,785 --> 00:09:45,986
It worried me sick.

221
00:09:46,087 --> 00:09:49,857
<i>♪ Now in a single moment</i>
<i>your past grows dim ♪</i>

222
00:09:49,957 --> 00:09:51,992
[Elvis] And I became
very discouraged.

223
00:09:52,093 --> 00:09:54,795
<i>♪ One thought goes racing</i>
<i>across your mind ♪</i>

224
00:09:54,895 --> 00:09:57,031
[announcer] One of the reasons
why Elvis has stayed around

225
00:09:57,131 --> 00:10:01,802
as long as he has, has been
due to a great mastermind

226
00:10:01,902 --> 00:10:04,238
of his manager,
Colonel Tom Parker.

227
00:10:04,338 --> 00:10:05,406
[Elvis]
<i>♪ With eyes ♪</i>

228
00:10:05,507 --> 00:10:07,341
<i>♪ That hide the man within ♪</i>

229
00:10:07,441 --> 00:10:09,410
[announcer]
Colonel Tom Parker...

230
00:10:09,511 --> 00:10:10,644
[Elvis]
<i>♪ You've lived and died ♪</i>

231
