884
00:47:23,410 --> 00:47:25,647
"A hunk, a hunk
of burning love" - twice!

885
00:47:25,747 --> 00:47:27,981
[imitates drumroll]
Drumroll!

886
00:47:28,717 --> 00:47:30,552
They didn't do it.

887
00:47:31,185 --> 00:47:33,688
[backup singers]
<i>♪ Burning love ♪</i>

888
00:47:33,788 --> 00:47:36,190
<i>♪ Burning love ♪</i>

889
00:47:37,925 --> 00:47:40,094
[laughing]

890
00:47:45,366 --> 00:47:48,502
-[musical flourish]
-[audience cheering]

891
00:47:48,603 --> 00:47:51,305
[speaking indistinctly]

892
00:47:52,106 --> 00:47:54,041
Thank you. You've been
a fantastic audience.

893
00:47:54,141 --> 00:47:55,242
Now that - that's a new one.

894
00:47:55,342 --> 00:47:56,910
We've never done it
on stage before,

895
00:47:57,010 --> 00:47:58,813
so if we goofed up, I'm sorry.

896
00:47:58,912 --> 00:48:01,248
<i>♪ I feel like a stranger ♪</i>

897
00:48:03,884 --> 00:48:07,321
<i>♪ Like a stranger</i>
<i>in my own hometown ♪</i>

898
00:48:07,421 --> 00:48:09,957
[crowd chattering]

899
00:48:10,057 --> 00:48:11,526
[woman screaming] Elvis!

900
00:48:11,626 --> 00:48:14,194
<i>♪ I feel like a stranger ♪</i>

901
00:48:16,564 --> 00:48:20,267
<i>♪ Like a stranger</i>
<i>in my own hometown ♪</i>

902
00:48:25,272 --> 00:48:28,710
<i>♪ All my so-called friends</i>
<i>stopped being friendly ♪</i>

903
00:48:29,343 --> 00:48:31,211
[Elvis] Yeah, I like these
midnight chills.

904
00:48:31,311 --> 00:48:33,347
<i>♪ Yeah, but you can't keep</i>
<i>a good man down ♪</i>

905
00:48:34,448 --> 00:48:36,518
[chattering]

906
00:48:39,119 --> 00:48:40,789
-[Elvis] I started to do it.
-[man] I didn't do it.

907
00:48:40,889 --> 00:48:42,289
[Elvis] But nobody heard me.

908
00:48:42,389 --> 00:48:43,957
-What, you did?
-Oh, yeah.

909
00:48:44,057 --> 00:48:45,426
I was expecting you to do it.

910
00:48:45,527 --> 00:48:47,695
No, I did the first
three or four lines of it, man,

911
00:48:47,796 --> 00:48:49,496
and nobody heard me.

912
00:48:49,597 --> 00:48:51,031
[man] Did you tell 'em
you were gonna do it?

913
00:48:51,131 --> 00:48:52,534
-Yeah.
-Did you tell yourself?

914
00:48:52,634 --> 00:48:54,334
-No.
-[laughter]

915
00:48:54,435 --> 00:48:56,604
[man] It look like
that little theatre...

916
00:48:56,704 --> 00:48:58,740
-It is the place you played.
-It is the place.

917
00:48:58,840 --> 00:49:00,174
-Yeah.
-Right.

918
00:49:00,274 --> 00:49:02,376
[Elvis] I played here
about twice, didn't I say?

919
00:49:02,476 --> 00:49:04,813
[man] Flock MC,
at the end of this street.

920
00:49:04,913 --> 00:49:06,246
[man] Grab a right here.

921
00:49:06,346 --> 00:49:07,715
That's when he first started
to manage me, right?

922
00:49:07,816 --> 00:49:08,750
[man] Yeah.

923
00:49:08,850 --> 00:49:10,484
The Colonel insisted

924
00:49:10,585 --> 00:49:12,319
that he have him
when he came back here.

925
00:49:12,419 --> 00:49:16,356
[man] The Colonel called
all the way to my place.

926
00:49:16,457 --> 00:49:19,026
He never forgets, man.
He never forgets anybody.

927
00:49:19,426 --> 00:49:21,763
He never forgets people.
He never forgets openings.

928
00:49:21,863 --> 00:49:24,866
-That's right.
-Or dates, birthdays.

929
00:49:25,567 --> 00:49:27,968
[Elvis] Colonel used to take
shows out on the road

930
00:49:28,068 --> 00:49:30,070
and he'd hire me for
an extra added singer

931
00:49:30,170 --> 00:49:32,507
and he undoubtedly liked
the performance that we did,

932
00:49:32,607 --> 00:49:35,108
so we decided to start
working together -

933
00:49:35,209 --> 00:49:36,911
him as my manager.

934
00:49:37,010 --> 00:49:38,880
-That's the Colonel.
-[laughter]

935
00:49:38,979 --> 00:49:40,347
-[man] That's his staff.
-Meet Colonel Parker.

936
00:49:40,447 --> 00:49:42,851
-That's his staff.
-Very thin.

937
00:49:43,217 --> 00:49:46,086
[unsettling music playing]

938
00:49:46,453 --> 00:49:48,322
[Elvis]
<i>♪ You look like an angel ♪</i>

939
00:49:48,422 --> 00:49:50,357
[backup singers]
<i>♪ Look like an angel ♪</i>

940
00:49:50,457 --> 00:49:52,594
[Elvis]
<i>♪ Walk like an angel ♪</i>

941
00:49:52,694 --> 00:49:54,328
[backup singers]
<i>♪ Walk like an angel ♪</i>

942
00:49:54,428 --> 00:49:56,764
[Elvis]
<i>♪ Talk like an angel ♪</i>

943
00:49:56,865 --> 00:50:00,501
<i>♪ But I got wise ♪</i>

944
00:50:00,602 --> 00:50:03,605
<i>♪ You're the devil</i>
<i>in disguise ♪</i>

945
00:50:03,705 --> 00:50:05,072
<i>♪ Oh, yes, you are ♪</i>

946
00:50:05,172 --> 00:50:07,609
<i>♪ Devil in disguise ♪</i>

947
00:50:07,842 --> 00:50:10,444
[reporter] Did you pick Parker
or did Parker come for you?

948
00:50:10,545 --> 00:50:12,614
[Elvis] We more or less
picked each other.

949
00:50:12,714 --> 00:50:14,582
You know, I was making
quite a bit of money,

950
00:50:14,682 --> 00:50:16,885
but, I mean, I wasn't as
nationally known as I am now.

951
00:50:16,985 --> 00:50:18,218
[reporter] Uh-huh.

952
00:50:18,318 --> 00:50:19,954
[Elvis] The Colonel
has a lot of friends

953
00:50:20,053 --> 00:50:22,089
in the entertainment business -
he had a lot of connections.

954
00:50:22,189 --> 00:50:23,257
[reporter] Oh, yeah.

955
00:50:23,357 --> 00:50:24,959
[Elvis] Moved with
lots of people

956
00:50:25,058 --> 00:50:26,761
that are important wheels
in the business.

957
00:50:26,861 --> 00:50:28,395
He's a very amusing guy

958
00:50:28,495 --> 00:50:31,331
and he plans stuff that nobody
else would even think of.

959
00:50:31,431 --> 00:50:33,535
I could tell you
lots of things.

960
00:50:33,635 --> 00:50:36,203
[man] Hi there.
How much are the dogs?

961
00:50:36,303 --> 00:50:39,239
[woman] We have
the large dogs for five dollars

962
00:50:39,339 --> 00:50:41,676
and the small dogs
for three dollars.

963
00:50:41,776 --> 00:50:43,945
[reporter] When you see
things sold on the street -

964
00:50:44,044 --> 00:50:45,747
some of them saying
"I like Elvis"

965
00:50:45,847 --> 00:50:47,347
and others saying
other things -

966
00:50:47,447 --> 00:50:49,584
do you get much for each time?

967
00:50:50,350 --> 00:50:52,052
Do you get a percentage

968
00:50:52,152 --> 00:50:53,688
when they sell an
"I Hate Elvis" button?

969
00:50:53,788 --> 00:50:55,489
[Elvis] To be truthful,
I really don't know.

970
00:50:55,590 --> 00:50:59,192
In fact, I don't know who sells
"I Hate Elvis" buttons.

971
00:50:59,293 --> 00:51:01,328
[reporter] Well, it's the same
man who sells the "I Like".

972
00:51:01,428 --> 00:51:03,731
-[audience cheering]
-[cameras clicking]

973
00:51:05,533 --> 00:51:08,068
There's so many places
that I haven't been yet.

974
00:51:08,168 --> 00:51:11,639
Like, I've never played
New York here, you know?

975
00:51:12,306 --> 00:51:14,308
I've never been to Britain
either, you know?

976
00:51:14,408 --> 00:51:15,610
[reporter speaking
indistinctly]

977
00:51:15,710 --> 00:51:18,012
I'd like to, yes, sir.
I'd like to very much.

978
00:51:18,111 --> 00:51:19,179
I'd like to go to Europe.

979
00:51:19,279 --> 00:51:21,181
I'd like to go to Japan
and all those places.

980
00:51:21,281 --> 00:51:22,750
I've never been
out of this country

981
00:51:22,850 --> 00:51:24,284
except in the service,
you know?

982
00:51:24,384 --> 00:51:26,721
<i>♪ Well, I've never</i>
<i>been to Spain ♪</i>

983
00:51:29,189 --> 00:51:32,727
<i>♪ But I kind of like</i>
<i>the music ♪</i>

984
00:51:34,428 --> 00:51:38,365
<i>♪ Say the ladies</i>
<i>are insane there ♪</i>

985
00:51:40,300 --> 00:51:43,638
<i>♪ And they sure know</i>
<i>how to use it ♪</i>

986
00:51:46,908 --> 00:51:49,309
<i>♪ They don't abuse it ♪</i>

987
00:51:49,844 --> 00:51:52,245
<i>♪ Never going to lose it ♪</i>

988
00:51:52,346 --> 00:51:54,882
<i>♪ I can't refuse it ♪</i>

989
00:51:56,818 --> 00:52:00,320
<i>♪ Well, I've never been</i>
<i>to England ♪</i>

990
00:52:00,922 --> 00:52:02,289
Whoo!

991
00:52:02,624 --> 00:52:06,460
<i>♪ But I kind of like</i>
<i>The Beatles ♪</i>

992
00:52:08,195 --> 00:52:11,666
<i>♪ So I headed for Las Vegas ♪</i>

993
00:52:13,601 --> 00:52:17,170
<i>♪ Only made it out</i>
<i>to Needles ♪</i>

994
00:52:20,041 --> 00:52:22,944
<i>♪ I got to feel it ♪</i>

995
00:52:23,044 --> 00:52:24,979
<i>♪ Must be near it ♪</i>

996
00:52:25,079 --> 00:52:28,116
<i>♪ Oh, it feels so good, Lord ♪</i>

997
00:52:28,215 --> 00:52:29,684
<i>♪ Feels so... ♪</i>

998
00:52:29,784 --> 00:52:33,353
<i>♪ Well, I've never</i>
<i>been to heaven ♪</i>

999
00:52:35,322 --> 00:52:38,793
<i>♪ But I've been to Oklahoma ♪</i>

1000
00:52:40,895 --> 00:52:44,264
<i>♪ Well, they tell me</i>
<i>I was born there ♪</i>

1001
00:52:46,100 --> 00:52:49,671
<i>♪ But I really don't remember ♪</i>

1002
00:52:52,573 --> 00:52:57,244
<i>♪ In Oklahoma or Arizona ♪</i>

1003
00:52:57,344 --> 00:53:00,548
<i>♪ Yeah, what does it matter? ♪</i>

1004
00:53:01,015 --> 00:53:03,084
<i>♪ What does it matter? ♪</i>

1005
00:53:03,450 --> 00:53:08,388
<i>♪ In Oklahoma or Arizona ♪</i>

1006
00:53:08,488 --> 00:53:11,425
<i>♪ Yeah, what does it matter? ♪</i>

1007
00:53:11,526 --> 00:53:13,895
<i>♪ What does it matter? ♪</i>

1008
00:53:22,103 --> 00:53:24,672
[audience cheering
and applauding]

1009
00:53:26,674 --> 00:53:32,379
[Elvis] Well, I'd like to do a
few oldies but goodies for you.

1010
00:53:32,479 --> 00:53:34,481
-[audience whooping]
-[chuckling]

1011
00:53:35,016 --> 00:53:37,217
If you'll wait
about 30 minutes.

1012
00:53:38,619 --> 00:53:40,121
[vocalises]

1013
00:53:40,722 --> 00:53:42,824
That's a funny-looking thing
up there, man.

1014
00:53:44,092 --> 00:53:45,727
I hope that thing don't fall.

1015
00:53:46,761 --> 00:53:48,096
[chuckling]

1016
00:53:48,462 --> 00:53:50,765
Flatter than a pancake, man.

1017
00:53:51,065 --> 00:53:52,834
[woman screaming] Elvis!

1018
00:53:52,934 --> 00:53:54,635
I'll get up in a minute,
just hang with us.

1019
00:53:54,736 --> 00:53:56,369
With the help of the
Jordanaires, friends,

1020
00:53:56,470 --> 00:54:00,174
we'd like to do one
called... "Love Me".

1021
00:54:00,541 --> 00:54:03,443
[guitar strums and stops]

1022
00:54:04,712 --> 00:54:06,313
It's the new one
on the end there.

1023
00:54:06,413 --> 00:54:08,516
[audience laughing]

1024
00:54:09,550 --> 00:54:13,588
<i>♪ Treat me like a fool ♪</i>

1025
00:54:13,688 --> 00:54:17,424
<i>♪ Treat me mean and cruel ♪</i>

1026
00:54:18,126 --> 00:54:20,928
<i>♪ But love me ♪</i>

1027
00:54:21,361 --> 00:54:23,097
Yeah...

1028
00:54:23,564 --> 00:54:26,834
<i>♪ Break my faithful heart ♪</i>

1029
00:54:26,934 --> 00:54:30,437
<i>♪ Tear it all apart ♪</i>

1030
00:54:30,538 --> 00:54:33,207
<i>♪ But love me ♪</i>

1031
00:54:33,306 --> 00:54:34,876
<i>♪ Won't you love me? ♪</i>

1032
00:54:34,976 --> 00:54:37,078
[audience cheering]

1033
00:54:37,178 --> 00:54:40,548
[Elvis]
<i>♪ I would beg and steal ♪</i>

1034
00:54:41,949 --> 00:54:46,654
<i>♪ Just to feel ♪</i>

1035
00:54:49,824 --> 00:54:54,361
<i>♪ Your heart ♪</i>

1036
00:54:56,030 --> 00:54:59,432
<i>♪ Beating close to mine ♪</i>

1037
00:55:05,273 --> 00:55:07,508
<i>♪ If you ever go ♪</i>

1038
00:55:07,608 --> 00:55:09,777
<i>♪ Darling, I'll be, oh ♪</i>

1039
00:55:10,912 --> 00:55:12,547
<i>♪ Oh, so lonely ♪</i>

1040
00:55:16,784 --> 00:55:20,588
<i>♪ I'll be sad and blue</i>
<i>Crying over you ♪</i>

1041
00:55:21,622 --> 00:55:23,991
[audience cheering
and whistling]

1042
00:55:25,760 --> 00:55:30,531
<i>-♪ I would beg and steal ♪</i>
<i>-♪ Beg and steal ♪</i>

1043
00:55:30,631 --> 00:55:35,536
<i>-♪ Just to feel ♪</i>
<i>-♪ Just to feel ♪</i>

1044
00:55:35,803 --> 00:55:40,675
<i>-♪ Your heart ♪</i>
<i>-♪ I want your heart ♪</i>

1045
00:55:40,775 --> 00:55:45,146
<i>-♪ Beating close to mine ♪</i>
<i>-♪ So close to mine ♪</i>

1046
00:55:45,246 --> 00:55:50,017
<i>♪ Oh, well, if you ever go ♪</i>

1047
00:55:50,117 --> 00:55:54,522
<i>♪ Darling, I'll be, oh ♪</i>

1048
00:55:54,622 --> 00:55:57,325
<i>♪ So lonely ♪</i>

1049
00:56:00,328 --> 00:56:03,363
<i>♪ Beggin' on my knees ♪</i>

1050
00:56:03,463 --> 00:56:07,500
<i>♪ All I ask is please ♪</i>

1051
00:56:07,602 --> 00:56:10,771
<i>♪ Please love me ♪</i>

1052
00:56:10,872 --> 00:56:15,943
<i>♪ Oh, yeah. ♪</i>

1053
00:56:18,145 --> 00:56:20,114
Whoo!

1054
00:56:20,748 --> 00:56:22,482
[reporter] You ever pull out
any of those old records

1055
00:56:22,583 --> 00:56:24,352
from the Sun label
and listen to them at all?

1056
00:56:24,451 --> 00:56:25,553
[laughing]

1057
00:56:25,653 --> 00:56:28,022
They sound funny, boy...

1058
00:56:28,723 --> 00:56:31,025
They got a lot of echo on 'em.
Man, I tell you.

1059
00:56:31,125 --> 00:56:34,195
<i>♪ Blue moon ♪</i>

1060
00:56:34,295 --> 00:56:38,866
<i>♪ You saw me standing alone ♪</i>

1061
00:56:39,466 --> 00:56:41,035
[Elvis]
In a lot of the mail I get,

1062
00:56:41,135 --> 00:56:43,504
people ask questions about
the kind of things I do

1063
00:56:43,604 --> 00:56:45,072
and all that sort of stuff.

1064
00:56:46,574 --> 00:56:48,142
Well, I don't smoke
and I don't drink

1065
00:56:48,242 --> 00:56:49,777
and I love to go to movies.

1066
00:56:51,345 --> 00:56:53,381
Maybe someday I'm going to have
a home and a family of my own

1067
00:56:53,480 --> 00:56:55,182
and I'm not going to
budge from it.

1068
00:57:00,655 --> 00:57:02,823
[Elvis humming]

1069
00:57:03,090 --> 00:57:03,925
[reporter] Are you satisfied

1070
00:57:04,025 --> 00:57:05,393
with the image
you've established?

1071
00:57:05,492 --> 00:57:06,560
Well, the image is one thing

1072
00:57:06,661 --> 00:57:08,629
and a human being is another,
you know?

1073
00:57:08,729 --> 00:57:10,531
[reporter] How close
is the image to the man?

1074
00:57:10,631 --> 00:57:12,499
It... it... it's very hard
to live up to an image.

1075
00:57:12,600 --> 00:57:14,068
I'll put it that way.

1076
00:57:14,769 --> 00:57:17,638
I've experienced a lot of
the different phases in life.

1077
00:57:17,738 --> 00:57:21,709
I've experienced happiness,
and loneliness and tragedy.

1078
00:57:21,809 --> 00:57:23,411
[reporter] What's that?

1079
00:57:23,511 --> 00:57:26,047
[Elvis] Losing my mother,
while I was in the army.

1080
00:57:26,147 --> 00:57:28,349
And although I think that
things like that,

1081
00:57:28,448 --> 00:57:29,984
as tragic as they are,

1082
00:57:30,084 --> 00:57:32,653
tend to make you a little
better human being, really.

1083
00:57:34,021 --> 00:57:38,125
<i>♪ And I miss her ♪</i>

1084
00:57:38,859 --> 00:57:42,663
<i>♪ Oh, how I miss her ♪</i>

1085
00:57:43,864 --> 00:57:47,635
<i>♪ Oh, how I miss her ♪</i>

1086
00:57:49,403 --> 00:57:52,540
<i>♪ Oh, how I miss her ♪</i>

1087
00:57:52,640 --> 00:57:56,177
<i>♪ And I always... ♪</i>

1088
00:57:56,277 --> 00:57:58,846
[song concludes]

1089
00:58:02,116 --> 00:58:03,985
[Elvis] I'm going to show
Joe that ending.

1090
00:58:04,752 --> 00:58:08,956
<i>♪ And I miss her ♪</i>

1091
00:58:09,056 --> 00:58:10,358
[band resumes playing]

1092
00:58:10,458 --> 00:58:14,662
<i>♪ How I miss her ♪</i>

1093
00:58:15,596 --> 00:58:18,966
<i>♪ Oh, how I miss her ♪</i>

1094
00:58:21,102 --> 00:58:24,271
<i>♪ And I miss her ♪</i>

1095
00:58:24,372 --> 00:58:28,809
<i>♪ Da, da, da, da, da, da ♪</i>

1096
00:58:33,214 --> 00:58:35,716
[audience cheering]

1097
00:58:37,218 --> 00:58:38,352
Now that you've seen me,

1098
00:58:38,452 --> 00:58:40,154
I'd like to take a look at you,
okay?

1099
00:58:40,254 --> 00:58:42,890
[Elvis] A funny thing happened
to me about a year ago.

1100
00:58:42,990 --> 00:58:45,993
Joe was showing me
how to go up on stage.

1101
00:58:46,093 --> 00:58:48,896
It was at intermission
and the lights were still on.

1102
00:58:48,996 --> 00:58:51,365
And I looked out
and I saw a crowd of people.

1103
00:58:51,465 --> 00:58:54,969
I got weak in the knees and all
of a sudden it just scared me.

1104
00:58:55,069 --> 00:58:56,137
You know, I...

1105
00:58:56,237 --> 00:58:58,539
It's funny because
I can't see you, really.

1106
00:58:58,639 --> 00:59:00,374
I can only see like
the first row here.

1107
00:59:00,474 --> 00:59:03,177
There's a lot of
folks out there.

1108
00:59:03,512 --> 00:59:05,813
-And out there, too.
-[crowd cheering loudly]

1109
00:59:05,913 --> 00:59:07,415
[reporter] Someone
just wrote an article

1110
00:59:07,516 --> 00:59:08,949
on The Rolling Stones,

1111
